<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching (Mus musculus (E11-E16.5 pseudoglandular embryonic lung airway tree under microfluidic transmural pressure control; fetal-sheep laryngeal physiology transferred for the valve model))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-5> ;
    schema:about "Mus musculus (E11-E16.5 pseudoglandular embryonic lung airway tree under microfluidic transmural pressure control; fetal-sheep laryngeal physiology transferred for the valve model)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D Navier-Stokes Stokesian fluid-structure interaction of individual ciliated epithelial cells, single-channel CaV1.2 gating kinetics, lobar branching programme sequences, or in-utero FBM pressure traces measured in the mouse",
        "does_not_claim: Saffman-Taylor viscous fingering or any Hele-Shaw interfacial instability (despite the file name and campaign slug, no viscous-fingering mathematics exists in the script); Gallus gallus data (the vendored specimen and all vendored references are Mus musculus and fetal sheep)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) 3D bifurcating tree grown inside an analytic ellipsoidal pleural cavity with 90-degree rotating bifurcation planes and pleura-contact tip arrest (`simulate_3d_pleural_cavity_lung_tree`), with a cavity-scale ablation 0.7-2.0 at 300 Pa (`evaluate_pleural_cavity_ablation`: contact fractions 0.50/0.50/0.25/0.00/0.00)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Laryngeal valve opening/closing cycles C dP/dt = Q - (P - P_amn)/R_larynx(t) integrated exactly per step over 48 h with an 11-point open-duty sweep (Spearman rho = -1.0, occlusion/open fold ratio 6.844 vs 6.728 reference) and the Jensen gap of the Hill branching rate (-0.0226 day^-1 at duty 0.40) (`simulate_laryngeal_valve_cycles`, `evaluate_laryngeal_duty_cycle_sweep`)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Spatially resolved CFTR/NKCC1 chloride secretion j_Cl(g) (geometric proximal-to-distal gradient, 6x) integrated over segment epithelial area and a Hagen-Poiseuille resistor-network luminal pressure solve P_node = P_amn + R_larynx Q_tot + sum_path R_i Q_i (`solve_tree_luminal_pressure`); intra-tree drop 6.0e-6 of the 200 Pa tracheal Delta P",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation (`segment_embryonic_lung_specimen`) of the vendored Mus musculus pseudoglandular E11-E16.5 embryonic lung specimen (`embryonic_lung_branching_specimen.jpg`, CC BY 3.0) extracting 17 distal terminal buds, distal-to-total airway area fraction = 0.6885, and mean distal tip radius = 3.8470 +- 1.3152 px",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Coupled 2D spatial microfluidic bronchial tree and Laplace wall stress solver (`simulate_2d_microfluidic_lung_tree`) plus 8-point Delta P in [0, 400] Pa sweep (`evaluate_transmural_pressure_sweep`), reproducing the vendored 48h terminal bud counts (Pearson r = 0.99997), branching rate Gamma_branch and ASM contraction frequency f_ASM columns",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact common-mode gauge invariance verification across (P_lumen, P_pleura) = (200, 0), (0, -200), and (500, 300) Pa (max deviation = 0.0000) for the 2D, 3D and valve solvers, alongside nifedipine Ca2+ channel blockade and tracheal drainage negative controls",
        "reported_in_source: Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell 34:668-681 & Nelson et al. (2017) nifedipine L-type Ca2+ channel blockade of ASM peristaltic contractions or tracheal intubation drainage (Delta P <= 0 Pa) collapsing terminal bud bifurcation",
        "reported_in_source: Laplace-Young circumferential epithelial wall stress sigma_theta = Delta P * R / h driving mechanosensitive FGF10/ERK1/2/Etv4 distal tip proliferation and bifurcation above critical threshold Delta P_c approx 50 Pa (Unbekandt et al. 2008 Mech. Dev. 125:314-324; Nelson et al. 2017)",
        "reported_in_source: Nelson, Gleghorn, Myers, Radisky & Stone (2017) Development 144:4328-4335 microfluidic chest cavity experiments proving that embryonic lung branching rate dN_tips/dt and synchronized airway smooth muscle (ASM) peristaltic wave frequency f_ASM depend strictly on the transmural pressure difference Delta P = P_lumen - P_pleura and are invariant under common-mode hydrostatic pressure shifts (P_lumen + P_0, P_pleura + P_0)",
        "reported_in_source: Olver & Strang (1974) chloride-driven fetal lung-liquid secretion with distal > proximal secretory activity; Harding et al. (1986) and Harding & Hooper (1996) fetal-sheep upper-airway resistance dominating lung-liquid efflux, a closed-glottis tracheal pressure plateau of 1-2 mmHg, and a laryngeal resistance drop during fetal breathing-movement episodes; Metzger et al. (2008) orthogonal bifurcation mode of the mouse bronchial tree",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D projected bronchial tree and continuum Laplace hoop stress field mapped to whole-mount E11.5-E16.5 pseudoglandular mouse lung explants in microfluidic chest chambers",
        "transfer_boundary: CFTR secretion is a prescribed functional form (geometric gradient), not a transcript-map-derived field; the laryngeal resistance in the 3D solver is back-solved so that the tracheal inlet pressure equals p_lumen_pa, so the tracheal Delta P is a boundary condition and only the intra-tree distribution is emergent",
        "transfer_boundary: The `*_obs` sweep columns of `tracheal_viscous_fingering_reference.json` are not literal digitisations of Nelson 2017 figures (no figure/table coordinates or digitisation provenance) and the Hill constants were fitted to them, so the Pearson r ~ 0.9999 correlations are largely self-referential",
        "transfer_boundary: The laryngeal valve / fetal-breathing-movement model transfers fetal-sheep in-utero physiology (Harding 1986/1996) to the explant setting of Nelson et al. (2017), whose cannulated explants have no larynx; the closed-glottis plateau (250 Pa), R_open/R_closed (0.25), duty (0.40), period (40 min) and tau_closed (6 min) are model choices flagged `provenance: model` in `pleural_cavity_valve_reference.json`",
        "transfer_boundary: The pleural cavity is an analytic ellipsoid (CAVITY_SEMI_AXES, CHEST_LENGTH_SCALE_UM = 1.6 mm) and not a stereolithographic STL chest mesh; no lobation or left-right asymmetry; generation depth of the 3D tree is inherited from the same 0-D Hill N(t) as the 2D solver, so the 3D tip count is a consistency check and not an emergent prediction" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Bifurcating vascular / bronchial / hyphal branch in Gallus gallus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "6. Tip-Splitting & Flow Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Bifurcating Vascular/Lung Trees" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Law r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
