<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 2 core (Delta P gauge, Laplace hoop stress, Hill bifurcation rate, ASM frequency; `compute_transmural_pressure` through `simulate_2d_microfluidic_lung_tree`, L153-362) is unchanged and the three Pass 3 mechanisms are implemented with the stated equations: Poiseuille resistor network with subtree-accumulated secretion (`solve_tree_luminal_pressure`, L428-477), 3D tree with 90-degree rotating bifurcation planes and ellipsoid clipping (`simulate_3d_pleural_cavity_lung_tree`, L480-620), and the valve ODE with exact-exponential update and the Jensen gap (`simulate_laryngeal_valve_cycles`, L635-691), all backed by 5 machine-checked Lean 4 laws (0 sorrys). Deductions: the 3D generation depth is set from the same 0-D `simulate_buds_48h` as the 2D solver (L497-499) and the per-tip Gamma(Delta P_tip) computed at L600 never feeds back into growth, so 3D confinement affects arrest only, not branching (-3); the laryngeal resistance is back-solved so that the tracheal inlet equals `p_lumen_pa` (L578-580), making the tracheal Delta P a boundary condition rather than an output of secretion vs. resistance (-2); the valve model is fetal-sheep in-utero physiology applied to a larynx-free explant system (-2); the file name and campaign slug promise Saffman-Taylor viscous fingering and the script contains none (L1-70 docstring lists Hill / Poiseuille / valve laws only) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py L495–L499: 3D generation depth derived from the 0-D Hill N(t) of simulate_buds_48h, so 3D tip count is inherited rather than emergent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py#L495-L499>",
        "2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py L573–L580: R_larynx back-solved so that the tracheal inlet pressure equals p_lumen_pa; tracheal Delta P is a boundary condition <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py#L573-L580>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L922-1112) now returns 16 reference-anchored measurements: the 9 Pass 2 metrics plus 7 Pass 3 metrics (FBM mean Delta P 154.3 Pa vs 200; duty-sweep Spearman rho = -1.0; occlusion/open fold ratio 6.844 vs the Nelson-derived 6.728 computed from the reference JSON at L943-945; Jensen gap -0.0226 day^-1; intra-tree Poiseuille drop 6.0e-6; 3D tip count 16 vs 2D 16; pleura-contact fraction 0.25 vs 0.0 unconfined). Deductions: specimen measurements 7-9 (L1082-1111) compare against the script's own self-recorded values (circular, by construction) (-4); the r ~ 0.9999 sweep correlations (measurements 1-3) are against `*_obs` columns that are fitted targets rather than digitised Nelson 2017 figure values, and the Hill constants (L98-108) were fitted to them (-3); measurement 15 (3D tips = 2D tips) is a consistency check since both inherit the same 0-D N(t), and measurement 16 uses the solver's own unconfined ablation as \"reference\" (-2); the FBM time-averaged Delta P (154.3 Pa) misses the 200 Pa reference by 23 % and the self-test tolerance at L1763 (100-280 Pa) is wide enough to pass it without comment (-2); the occlusion/open ratio reference (6.728) is a ratio of two fitted `*_obs` values, not a measured occlusion-vs-drainage quantity (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
