<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — Source and data traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/` now carries 9 BibTeX entries (`paper_citations.bib` L1-104), the SHA-256-pinned specimen and reference JSON verified at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L115-147), and the new `pleural_cavity_valve_reference.json` (85 lines) which flags every Pass 3 constant as `provenance: literature` or `provenance: model` and records `doi_verified_offline: false` for the four new citations. Deductions: the four new DOIs (Olver & Strang 1974, Harding et al. 1986, Harding & Hooper 1996, Metzger et al. 2008) were recorded from memory and could not be verified offline in this pass (bib `note` fields L56, L68, L80, L92) (-4); McCray et al. 1992 is cited in a code comment (L381) with no bib entry (-1); the cavity geometry (`CAVITY_SEMI_AXES`, `CAVITY_CENTER`, `CHEST_LENGTH_SCALE_UM`, L389-391) and the secretion magnitudes (`J_CL_*`, L393-394) are unsourced model choices, and `P_CLOSED_GLOTTIS_PLATEAU_PA` = 250 Pa was chosen inside the Harding & Hooper 1-2 mmHg range to coincide with the Pass 2 JSON's 250 Pa occlusion regime (-3); the `*_obs` sweep columns carry no figure/table digitisation provenance (Pass 2 carry-over) (-2); the campaign-level seed paper (Nelson 2015, 10.1242/dev.119123, Gallus gallus) does not match the modelled sources (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py L378–L381: McCray et al. 1992 cited in a comment without a corresponding bib entry <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py#L378-L381>",
        "2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py L389–L399: Cavity semi-axes, chest scale, J_Cl magnitudes, closed-glottis plateau, R_open/R_closed, FBM period and tau_closed: model choices, only partially literature-ranged <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py#L389-L399>",
        "datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/paper_citations.bib L47–L92: olver1974, harding1986, harding1996, metzger2008 entries, each with note 'DOI not verified offline (Pass 3)' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/datasets/tracheal_viscous_fingering/paper_citations.bib#L47-L92>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-source-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The vendored Mus musculus E11-E16.5 pseudoglandular specimen is SHA-256-verified and segmented by `segment_embryonic_lung_specimen` (L860-915) into 17 terminal buds with tip radii; Panel F of the 3x3 figure overlays the segmentation on the micrograph; the new Panel G and the dedicated 3D figure (`render_pleural_cavity_figure`, L1530-1575) show the tree confined by the ellipsoid, and the GIF (`render_growth_gif`, L1578-1670) adds a rotating 3D pane with larynx OPEN/CLOSED annotation. Deductions: the \"reference\" morphometrics the specimen is compared against (17 buds, 0.6885, 3.8470 px) are the script's own earlier outputs recorded into the reference JSON, so the match is by construction (-4); the pleural cavity is an analytic ellipsoid without lobation or left-right asymmetry, so the 3D panels do not resemble a mouse thorax or any imaged chest cavity (-3); the 3D panes use default matplotlib 3D axes and are visually sparse, and the Panel E legend still overlaps the bars (Pass 2 carry-over) (-2); the dispatch/campaign organism (Gallus gallus) is not represented by any vendored specimen (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py L1082–L1111: Specimen measurements 7-9 compare segmentation outputs against reference_value 17.0 / 0.6885 / 3.8470, which are the script's own recorded outputs (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py#L1082-L1111>",
        "docs/media/tracheal_viscous_fingering_pleural_cavity_3d.png (generated output, not in repo): Ellipsoid, not a lobated chest mesh; no left/right lobe asymmetry — docs/media/tracheal_viscous_fingering_pleural_cavity_3d.png: rendered output of 2015-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering.py at 171769b9, image/png, 451516 B, 2822×832 px, artifact_sha256 d88b84058ecf5d86635593a5569c5e1559592c5d59e3a787fd599c07b25b2d9c (sha256 d88b84058ecf5d86635593a5569c5e1559592c5d59e3a787fd599c07b25b2d9c), spec_fingerprint b14c2a9f28075322a3f6f059ad4e5c0d7c9dc62fb5a6e7b4d98bf273506f3edc" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

